# Root Cause and Proposed Fix

**Root Cause:** [1][2] The hover glow regression was caused by overlapping CSS box-shadows—one from the component hover token and one from an outer focus ring variable. This resulted in double outlines on icon buttons, particularly in high-contrast mode with reduced motion. [2] The stacked shadows briefly showed as double outlines when moving the pointer or programmatically toggling loading state.

**Proposed Change:** [1] The approach proposed was to move both shadows to theme variables and dedupe by expressing focus as outline rather than stacked shadow for compact/icon buttons. 

Additionally, [5] a CSS solution was suggested to handle high-contrast modes specifically:
```css
.icon-btn:focus { outline: none; box-shadow: var(--focus-shadow); }
@media (forced-colors: active) { 
  .icon-btn:focus { box-shadow: none; outline: 2px solid Highlight; } 
}
```

This ensures that in forced-colors/high-contrast mode, the system outline is used instead of the custom shadow to avoid the stacking artifacts [5].
